.TH OPENWITTY 1 "October 2026" "openwitty 0.1.0-alpha.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openwitty \- unofficial, experimental control application for the LEWITT CONNECT 2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openwitty
.RB [ \-\-mock "] [" \-\-show " page] [" \-\-screenshot " file] [" \-\-size " WxH] [" \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Qt 6 / QML control application for the LEWITT CONNECT 2 USB audio interface. It is an
independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by LEWITT, and not a replacement for
LEWITT CONTROL CENTER.
.PP
Connected to a real CONNECT 2 it shows the device state (inputs, outputs, meters, the selected
channel) read-only. It changes the device only for the speaker and headphone volume and mute,
and only after the user has turned on and confirmed \fISpeaker/headphone control\fR in
Settings. Firmware update and factory reset are not implemented. A simulated device is
included and always labelled as simulated.
.PP
Settings \(-> Desktop integration shows whether the desktop hardware volume is available, explains
the optional kernel compatibility quirk, and can keep the desktop (KDE/PipeWire) volume in step
with the speaker volume knob, also in the background through the
.BR openwitty-volumed (1)
user service, and can add an optional status icon to the system tray
.RB ( openwitty-tray (1)).
.PP
Only one window runs per desktop session: starting OpenWitty again (launcher, tray icon) brings the open
window to the front, on the requested page, and the second start exits. Closing the window ends it and
releases the device; the background service, if enabled, keeps running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-mock
Start with the simulated device.
.TP
.BI \-\-show " page"
Open settings, settings-device, settings-desktop, wizard or onboarding at start.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " file"
Render one frame to a PNG and exit (offscreen use).
.TP
.BI \-\-size " WxH"
Window size for screenshots.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostic\-legacy\-polling
Diagnostic: use the former 2 Hz settings / 4 Hz status polling.
.TP
.BI \-\-quit\-after\-seconds " n"
Diagnostic: quit normally after n seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-hw\-check
Diagnostic for owner-approved hardware tests: records a settings baseline when the device connects and
reports, on standard error and under Settings \(-> Device control, which settings changed after each
write and on request (\(lqCompare with baseline\(rq). Read-only; it uses the window's own device
connection, so no second program competes for the device. It prints field names, offsets and the old and
new values of the changed settings bytes only; no device identifiers and no full settings dump. The baseline
comes from the first
successful settings read (also after a hand-over from the background service) and is never replaced
without the explicit \(lqReplace baseline\(rq confirmation; until it exists, no device write is sent.
Takes effect only when the
window starts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/openwitty/openwitty.conf
Desktop integration settings (default \fI~/.config/openwitty/openwitty.conf\fR), shared with
.BR openwitty-volumed (1).
Deleting it restores the defaults (everything off).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openwitty-cli (1),
